# String builder and byte reader

Stateful accumulator and cursor objects — a StringBuilder (incremental string construction) and a
ByteReader (positional read over a byte sequence) — modelled as LOGOS structs threaded functionally,
so they run byte-identically on every tier. The counterpart of Go's strings.Builder / bytes.Reader.
Auto-imported on reference.

## Note
A StringBuilder accumulates text as a `parts` sequence of Text fragments, joined only when the final string is materialized.

## A StringBuilder has:
    a parts, which is Seq of Text.

## Note
Creates an empty StringBuilder with a fresh, empty `parts` sequence.

## To newBuilder () -> StringBuilder:
    Return a new StringBuilder with parts (a new Seq of Text).

## Note
Appends text `s` to the builder by pushing it onto `parts`, returning the updated StringBuilder.

## To builderWriteString (b: StringBuilder, s: Text) -> StringBuilder:
    Let ps be b's parts.
    Push s to ps.
    Return a new StringBuilder with parts ps.

## Note
Materializes the accumulated text by concatenating every fragment in `parts` in order.

## To builderString (b: StringBuilder) -> Text:
    Let mutable out be "".
    Repeat for s in (b's parts):
        Set out to out combined with s.
    Return out.

## Note
Returns the total length of the builder by summing the length of every fragment in `parts`.

## To builderLen (b: StringBuilder) -> Int:
    Let mutable total be 0.
    Repeat for s in (b's parts):
        Set total to total + (length of s).
    Return total.

## Note
Clears the builder, returning a fresh StringBuilder with an empty `parts` sequence.

## To builderReset (b: StringBuilder) -> StringBuilder:
    Return a new StringBuilder with parts (a new Seq of Text).

## Note
A ByteReader holds a `data` byte sequence and a 1-based cursor `pos` marking the next byte to read.

## A ByteReader has:
    a data, which is Seq of Int.
    a pos, which is Int.

## Note
Creates a ByteReader over byte sequence `xs` with the cursor positioned at the first byte (`pos` 1).

## To newReader (xs: Seq of Int) -> ByteReader:
    Return a new ByteReader with data xs and pos 1.

## Note
Returns the byte at the current cursor position without advancing the cursor.

## To readerReadByte (r: ByteReader) -> Int:
    Return item (r's pos) of (r's data).

## Note
Moves the cursor forward by one byte, returning an updated ByteReader over the same data.

## To readerAdvance (r: ByteReader) -> ByteReader:
    Return a new ByteReader with data (r's data) and pos (r's pos + 1).

## Note
Reports whether the cursor still points at a byte, i.e. `pos` is at most the data length.

## To readerHasMore (r: ByteReader) -> Bool:
    Return r's pos is at most (length of r's data).

## Note
Returns the number of bytes remaining from the cursor to the end of the data.

## To readerLen (r: ByteReader) -> Int:
    Return (length of r's data) - r's pos + 1.

## Note
Rewinds the cursor back to the first byte (`pos` 1) over the same data.

## To readerReset (r: ByteReader) -> ByteReader:
    Return a new ByteReader with data (r's data) and pos 1.

## Note
A no-op capacity hint that returns the builder unchanged, since `parts` grows on demand.

## To builderGrow (b: StringBuilder, n: Int) -> StringBuilder:
    Return b.

## Note
Moves the cursor to an absolute position `p` over the same data.

## To readerSeek (r: ByteReader, p: Int) -> ByteReader:
    Return a new ByteReader with data (r's data) and pos p.

## Note
Appends a single byte by converting code `c` to its character via `chr` and writing it as text.

## To builderWriteByte (b: StringBuilder, c: Int) -> StringBuilder:
    Return builderWriteString(b, chr(c)).

## Note
Returns the builder's accumulated text as a byte sequence via `text_bytes`.

## To builderBytes (b: StringBuilder) -> Seq of Int:
    Return text_bytes(builderString(b)).

## Note
Returns a new builder holding only the first `n` bytes of the accumulated text.

## To builderTruncate (b: StringBuilder, n: Int) -> StringBuilder:
    Let sb be text_bytes(builderString(b)).
    Let out be a new Seq of Int.
    Let mutable i be 1.
    While i is at most n:
        Push item i of sb to out.
        Set i to i + 1.
    Return builderWriteString(newBuilder(), text_from_bytes(out)).

## Note
Returns the total length of the underlying data, independent of the cursor position.

## To readerSize (r: ByteReader) -> Int:
    Return length of r's data.

## Note
Steps the cursor back by one byte, undoing a prior advance over the same data.

## To readerUnreadByte (r: ByteReader) -> ByteReader:
    Return a new ByteReader with data (r's data) and pos (r's pos - 1).

## Note
Returns up to `n` bytes starting at the cursor, stopping at the end of the data if fewer remain.

## To readerNext (r: ByteReader, n: Int) -> Seq of Int:
    Let out be a new Seq of Int.
    Let mutable i be 0.
    While i is less than n:
        Let idx be r's pos + i.
        If idx is at most (length of r's data):
            Push item idx of (r's data) to out.
        Set i to i + 1.
    Return out.
